+# Worker session brief (D-092)
+
+You are a worker session on Flottila. The coordinator (the architect of the main campaign) gave
+you one BACKLOG row, a base commit and the allowed paths. For this one row you are the task
+architect: read `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `docs/WORKFLOW.md` §1 and §11 and the row, then run the
+loop of §1 steps 3–6 for it — acceptance spec, test-author (red observed), your approval of the
+tests, task packet, implementer, verifier (`mvn -B -ntp verify -Pit`, coverage check against the
+base commit, scoped PIT), reviewer — with the model and effort of the row's class.
+
+Done for you is: review PASS, then **one** commit on branch `claude/w-<task id>` (Conventional
+Commits, the row's `Task:` trailer, the trailers of `docs/WORKFLOW.md` §3), pushed with
+`git push -u origin claude/w-<task id>`, and the handback file `agent/handbacks/<task id>.md`
+inside that commit.
+
+The handback file, at most 40 lines: the PROGRESS entry as you would write it (format in
+`docs/WORKFLOW.md` §2, commit hash left as `<integrate>`), every evidence line with its log path,
+the reviewer's verdict and reasons, the coverage figures of the touched modules, and any
+**proposed** D-line or finding as text without a number (the coordinator numbers it).
+
+Leave to the coordinator, always: `agent/BACKLOG.md`, `agent/HANDOFF.md`, `agent/NOTES.md`,
+`PROGRESS.md`, `docs/DECISIONS.md`, `docs/findings/`, `ci/coverage-baseline.json`, `main`, and
+every path outside the allowed paths. A change the row needs outside them is a stop: write it in
+the handback as blocked, with the path and why, commit what is reviewed, push, and end.
+
+Never ask the owner; never start another session. If the row turns out harder than its class (a
+second review FAIL, a design question the row did not settle), stop with a partial handback marked
+`raise to C` — the coordinator takes the row back into its serial loop.
