+## 11. Parallel worker sessions (D-092, pilot)
+
+Two worker sessions run tasks beside the architect, each in its own cloud container (own CPU, own
+tree); the architect becomes the **coordinator**: it selects, briefs, integrates and keeps the
+ledger. Inside every session the limits of `AGENTS.md` still hold (two subagents, one writer).
+
+1. **Select.** Up to two `ready` rows that can run side by side: class A or B; disjoint modules and
+   files (compare the allowed paths of the packets); no bench or gate measurement; no change to
+   `pom.xml` module structure, ArchUnit rules, `.claude/`, `ci/coverage-baseline.json` or a
+   public type in `flottila-api`; neither depends on the other. Class C, gate rows, FIX rows for a
+   red `main` and anything touching a shared file stay in the coordinator's own serial loop.
+2. **Brief.** One `create_session` per row, prompt = `agent/WORKER.md` + the row id + the base
+   commit + the allowed paths, `outcome_branch: claude/w-<task id>`. The row is set `in-progress`
+   with `worker: claude/w-<task id>` in the coordinator's next ledger commit.
+3. **Wait without polling.** The coordinator does integration or ledger work meanwhile; with
+   nothing else to do it sets one `send_later` check-in per worker at the expected duration (the
+   only scheduled wake-up D-092 allows) and reads `get_session` (`status_bucket`) then — never a
+   sleep, never a loop. A worker that is `failed`, or idle without its handback, is read through
+   `list_events` and either resumed with one `send_message` or its row returned to `ready`.
+4. **Integrate, one worker at a time.** Fetch the branch; cherry-pick its commit onto current
+   `main`; the verifier runs `mvn -B -ntp verify -Pit` and the coverage check on the rebased tree;
+   the reviewer reads the rebased diff only where the rebase changed it (else the worker's review
+   PASS stands). Then the coordinator writes the coverage baseline (`--write`), the PROGRESS entry
+   from the handback, the BACKLOG status and HANDOFF, assigns the numbers of any proposed D-line
+   or finding, and commits **one** commit per task to `main` with the usual trailers. A conflict
+   or a red re-verify goes back to the worker by `send_message` with the failing section, or the
+   row returns to `ready` with the reason.
+5. **Measure the pilot.** Per task: wall time from brief to integration, review rounds, and tokens
+   where the session reports them (else `ENVIRONMENT_BLOCKED`), against the last comparable
+   single-session tasks in PROGRESS. The numbers go to `bench/RESULTS.md` §D-092 pilot. The pilot
+   ends after four integrated tasks; the owner decides on continuing from that section.
+
+A worker never edits the ledger (`agent/BACKLOG.md`, `agent/HANDOFF.md`, `agent/NOTES.md`,
+`PROGRESS.md`, `docs/DECISIONS.md`, `docs/findings/`), `ci/coverage-baseline.json` or `main`;
+it proposes, the coordinator records.
